   "text": {
    "L1": "Perimeter is the total length of the boundary of a closed shape.",
    "L2": "So we go all the way around and add every side. It is a length, so we use centimetres, metres or kilometres.",
    "L3": "For a rectangle, there are two equal lengths and two equal breadths.",
    "L4": "That gives the formula 2 × (length + breadth), not length plus breadth just once.",
    "L5": "For 8 centimetres by 5 centimetres, the perimeter is 2 × (8 + 5), which is 26 centimetres.",
    "L6": "In the worked example, one round of a 50 metre by 30 metre park is 160 metres.",
    "L7": "Three rounds are 3 × 160, or 480 metres. For a square, use 4 × side, and count every side of an irregular shape.",
    "L8": "Now choose the perimeter of the 8 centimetre by 5 centimetre rectangle."
   },
